    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0397" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1669.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-02T11:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 2, 1915—11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I learn that present trouble in Puerto Plata is to determine whether the
                    professional revolutionist need fear American suppression. I recommend prompt
                    and vigorous suppression of this disturbance by the Department. I believe that
                    any hesitation to keep our promise of peace to the Dominican Republic will mean
                    another general revolution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
